WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.075
The first card represents Daniel’s incoming request. A supplier wants a morning

00:00:05.075 --> 00:00:10.150
slot, and a virtual client discussion may move to a physical lunch.

00:00:10.150 --> 00:00:15.225
The second card reminds us that these are not accepted changes.

00:00:15.467 --> 00:00:19.875
The diary contains existing commitments. The supplier claims approval, but Daniel has

00:00:19.875 --> 00:00:24.283
not verified it. Accepted arrangements for the afternoon visit do not automatically

00:00:24.283 --> 00:00:28.692
cover lunch.

00:00:28.933 --> 00:00:33.008
Before opening the guidance, write what Daniel can do now. Name two

00:00:33.008 --> 00:00:37.083
unknowns and identify whose decision or acceptance is still needed. You may

00:00:37.083 --> 00:00:41.158
improve this response later.
